\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,33);
\foreach \t in {0,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,0) {$\t$};
\foreach \d in {6,12,18,24,30} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\d) {$\d$};
\node[below] at (2,-5) {Time (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,15) {Distance from home (km)};
\draw[blue,line width=0.8pt] (0,0)--(2,24)--(2.5,24)--(3.5,0);
\foreach \t/\d in {0/0,2/24,2.5/24,3.5/0} \fill[blue] (\t,\d) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The initial point is $(0,600)$ because the vehicle starts away from the depot. Arrival is $(3,0)$. Plot these points and join with a straight line sloping down.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.05cm,y=0.004cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]
