The outward stage ends at $(1,60)$ and the stop ends at $(1.5,60)$.
$t=\frac{d}{s}=\frac{60}{30}=2\text{ h}$.
The return ends after $1.5+2=3.5$ hours, at $(3.5,0)$. Plot these with $(0,0)$ and join consecutive points.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.05cm,y=0.04cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[housegrid,line width=0.25pt,xstep=0.5,ystep=10] (0,0) grid (4,80);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,88);
\foreach \t in {0,1,2,3,4} \node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\t,0) {$\t$};
\foreach \d in {20,40,60,80} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\d) {$\d$};
\node[below] at (2,-13) {Time (hours)};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,40) {Distance from home (km)};
\draw[blue,line width=0.8pt] (0,0)--(1,60)--(1.5,60)--(3.5,0);
\foreach \t/\d in {0/0,1/60,1.5/60,3.5/0} \fill[blue] (\t,\d) circle (1.5pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use hours when multiplying by speeds in km/h.
$d_1=st=60\times\frac{20}{60}=20\text{ km}$.
$d_2=st=40\times1.25=50\text{ km}$.
The first stage ends at $(20,20)$ and the stop ends at $(35,20)$. The final time is $20+15+75=110$ minutes and the final distance is $20+50=70$ km. Plot $(0,0)$, $(20,20)$, $(35,20)$ and $(110,70)$, then join consecutive points.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[]}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.035cm,y=0.04cm,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black]
